core3h_time - Core3H board time (DBBC3 rack)

Syntax:   core3h_time=board

Response: core3h_time/board,epoch,seconds,days,time,(nominal),difference

Settable parameters:

board:      board to read, 1 to the number of IFs specified in
            'dbbc3.ctl. (nominal maximum 8). No default. The previous
            value is not available with '*'.

Monitor only parameter:

epoch       VDIF epoch (halfYearsSince2000); the value for January
            1-June 30, 2020 should be '0'

seconds     seconds since epoch

days        full days since the start of 2000 until the epoch date
            (daysSince2000); the value for January 1-June 30, 2020
            should be '0'

time        board date/time in format YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss

nominal     nominal VDIF epoch for board 'time', shown in parentheses

difference  board time minus FS time in seconds, positive if the board
            leads the FS

Comments:

All dates and times are UTC.

This command samples the 'time' of Core3H 'board' at the start of the
next UTC second.

It may take more than one second for the board to respond. As a
result, the board 'time' shown may not match the FS log time stamp.
However, 'difference' is calculated as the FS time when the request
was made and the board time returned. If it is zero, they agree at the
one second level.

Another consequence of the board sometimes taking more than one second
to respond is that consecutive 'core3H_mode=...' commands may not
return board times that are consecutive.

The Core3H board's labels for 'epoch' and 'days' are shown in the
Monitor only parameters list in parentheses.

The 'nominal' value is not returned by the board. It is calculated
based on the board 'time' and displayed for informational purposes.

The VDIF epoch is described by this section from the VDIF
specification:

  Reference epoch: [It is] ... the 6-month period in which the VDIF
  clock was set, with an origin of at 00UTC 1 Jan 2000, such that ‘0’
  corresponds to the first 6 months of 2000, ‘1’ corresponds to the 6
  months starting 00H 1 July 2000, etc. After setting, [it] ... is
  static and is not incremented. [It] ... rolls over to 0 again when
  the reference epoch corresponds to the 6-month period starting 00H 1
  Jan 2032.

NOTE: Some DBBC3 firmware versions may automatically increment the
epoch value at the start of a new 6-month period.
